QnVoice Cebuano voice model sources

Cebuano speech uses the app’s shared VoxCPM2 BaseLM Q4_K_M and Q8_0 acoustic model. OpenBMB and ModelBest release VoxCPM2 under Apache 2.0. The model weights and licenses are attributed under Filipino model licenses in Settings.
https://huggingface.co/openbmb/VoxCPM2

Cebuano shares the original synthetic reference and precomputed AudioVAE features used by QnVoice for Filipino. The reference was generated with mlx-community/VoxCPM2-4bit at revision dc9e5c187858da5f4a13dc4c247e297339216381.
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24022271

English-to-Cebuano translation uses Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-ceb under Apache 2.0. QnVoice exports it to ONNX, dynamically quantizes supported weights to int8 and extracts the Marian tokenizer assets.
https://huggingface.co/Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-ceb/tree/e94aee550a4d15c5b5da28a4be4fb2cb0dede50a

The bundled translation and synthesis run on the device.
